{
  "_doc": [
    "The served event (quota-model 65 §7, with 66 §1's head_at and readings), as the proxy sends it on POST /reports and the brain takes it.",
    "Both sides' tests read this file. The proxy's encoder emits exactly the keys of `event` in the applied cases, every one of them, null where unknown.",
    "The brain answers each case, applied in order, as `result` says; prices it as `api_usd` says (USD at the list prices of 2026-11-03, rounded to 6 places; null = unpriced, with `unpriced` the reason's start); and counts `seq` gaps per boot.",
    "Accounts are named by provider: the brain's test maps anthropic-1, codex-1 and kimi-1 to accounts of that provider in its harness. unknown-acct is no account.",
    "Each `refused` case is the `refused_base` case's event with a fresh id, then its `patch` (keys replaced), `drop` (keys removed) or `read_at_ahead_s` (read_at that far ahead of the brain's clock). The brain answers each `refused`, with a why.",
    "head_at is when the response's head reached the proxy, at or before read_at. readings are that head's window readings that carry a use, keyed by the brain's window ids as the `reading` report names them (five_hour, seven_day, scoped:<DisplayName>, window:<period>, and window:<period>#n for a second codex window of one length), each {used_pct, resets_at}, resets_at null where the header didn't carry it. readings is {} when the head carried no such window: no rate-limit headers (Kimi), only unmapped or status-only windows, or a codex head with only its credits. An incomplete event carries both.",
    "output_max is the request's max_tokens on an incomplete event whose client hung up or whose stream the upstream cut, with its input counted, no output count and no server-side tool named; null otherwise. The brain counts the event in sizing within that bound and leaves it unpriced (66 §4).",
    "Cache writes go by lifetime: Anthropic's 5m and 1h, OpenAI's 30m and 12h. cache_write is a total whose lifetimes are unknown; the brain leaves it unpriced.",
    "A model priced by prompt length (OpenAI's over 272K tokens, Claude Haiku 5.5's over 100K) pays its higher prices for every token of a request whose prompt is over: input, cache writes and cache reads.",
    "Hand-written 2026-11-03; head_at, readings and their cases added 2026-11-03 (66 §1, push 2); required, with their missing-key cases, 2026-11-04 (push 3). output_max and its cases added 2026-11-04 (66 §1, push 5); required, with its missing-key case, 2026-11-04 (push 6). Prices: docs/quota-model 10 (Anthropic), 11 (codex), 12 (Kimi)."
  ],
